---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { SEGMENT_POINTS, SEGMENTS_BY_DIGIT } from "../../lib/hammingGame";
import { LEARN_TOPICS, getAdjacentLearnTopics } from "../../lib/learnTopics";

const CURRENT_HREF = "/learn/error-correction";
const currentTopic = LEARN_TOPICS.find((topic) => topic.href === CURRENT_HREF)!;
const { prev, next } = getAdjacentLearnTopics(CURRENT_HREF);

const before = "10110010";
const flipIndex = 5;
const after = before
	.split("")
	.map((bit, i) => (i === flipIndex ? (bit === "1" ? "0" : "1") : bit))
	.join("");

const realWorldExamples = [
	{
		name: "Satellites",
		text: "sending data across huge distances, where interference is common and re-sending data is slow or expensive",
	},
	{
		name: "Computer memory (RAM)",
		text: "many servers use error-correcting memory that silently fixes the occasional flipped bit, caused by things as small as background radiation",
	},
	{
		name: "QR codes and barcodes",
		text: "built to stay scannable even when part of the code is smudged, torn, or dirty",
	},
	{
		name: "CDs and DVDs",
		text: "able to keep playing even with small scratches on the disc",
	},
];
---

<Layout
	title="Error Correction, Explained"
	description="How computers detect and fix corrupted data using Hamming distance and check bits — the same idea behind every LogicDash guess."
	ogType="article"
>
	<p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/learn">Learn</a> / {currentTopic.title}</p>

	<section class="hero">
		<h1>Error Correction, Explained</h1>
		<p class="hero-lead">
			Hamming distance isn't just a game mechanic. It's how computers catch their own mistakes.
		</p>
	</section>

	<div class="blocks">
		<section class="block">
			<p class="block-title">The Problem: Data Gets Corrupted</p>
			<p class="block-text">
				Every time data moves — through the air to a satellite, across a network cable, sitting in
				your phone's memory — there's a small chance a bit flips by accident. A 0 becomes a 1, or a
				1 becomes a 0. Usually caused by things like electrical interference, cosmic radiation, or a
				weak signal.
			</p>
			<p class="block-text">
				For a single wrong digit, that might not sound serious. But multiply it across billions of
				bits, and errors become inevitable. Computers need a way to catch them — and ideally, fix
				them — automatically.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="block block--example">
			<p class="block-title">The Idea: Add a Few Extra Bits</p>
			<p class="block-text">
				In the 1940s, a mathematician named Richard Hamming came up with a clever trick. Instead of
				just sending your data as-is, you add a small number of extra bits, calculated from the
				original data. These extra bits don't carry new information — they exist purely to check the
				rest.
			</p>
			<p class="block-text">
				If a bit gets flipped in transmission, those extra "check" bits won't line up anymore. And
				because of exactly where the mismatch shows up, the receiving computer can work out precisely
				which bit was wrong — and flip it back. No retransmission needed.
			</p>

			<div class="compare-stack">
				{
					[
						{ label: "Before", bits: before },
						{ label: "After", bits: after },
					].map((row) => (
						<div class="compare-labeled-row">
							<span class="compare-row-label">{row.label}</span>
							<div class="compare-row">
								{row.bits.split("").map((bit, i) => (
									<span
										class={`compare-tile ${bit === "1" ? "compare-tile--on" : ""} ${i === flipIndex ? "compare-tile--diff" : ""}`}
									>
										<svg class="compare-digit" viewBox="0 0 60 100" aria-hidden="true">
											{Object.entries(SEGMENT_POINTS).map(([seg, points]) => (
												<polygon
													class={`compare-segment ${SEGMENTS_BY_DIGIT[bit]?.includes(seg) ? "is-on" : ""}`}
													points={points}
												/>
											))}
										</svg>
									</span>
								))}
							</div>
						</div>
					))
				}
			</div>
			<p class="compare-caption">The highlighted bit is the one that flipped.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<p class="block-title">This Is the Same Idea as LogicDash</p>
			<p class="block-text">
				Sound familiar? It's the same core concept you use every time you play. In the game, you're
				told how many bits differ from the secret, and you use logic to figure out which ones. Real
				error-correcting codes do something similar, just automated — the extra check bits let a
				computer instantly pinpoint the flipped bit, without a human needing to guess at all.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<p class="block-title">Where This Shows Up in Real Life</p>
			<ul class="unit-list">
				{
					realWorldExamples.map((example) => (
						<li>
							<span class="example-name">{example.name}</span> — {example.text}
						</li>
					))
				}
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<div class="learn-pagination">
				{
					prev && (
						<a class="learn-pagination-link learn-pagination-prev" href={prev.href}>
							← {prev.title}
						</a>
					)
				}
				{
					next &&
						(next.live ? (
							<a class="learn-pagination-link learn-pagination-next" href={next.href}>
								{next.title} →
							</a>
						) : (
							<span class="learn-pagination-link learn-pagination-next learn-pagination-soon">
								{next.title} (coming soon)
							</span>
						))
				}
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.breadcrumb {
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
		text-align: center;
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
	}

	.breadcrumb a {
		color: #ffae2e;
		font-weight: 600;
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	.breadcrumb a:hover {
		text-decoration: underline;
	}

	.hero {
		text-align: center;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	.hero h1 {
		margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
		font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 5vw, 2.1rem);
	}

	.hero-lead {
		margin: 0 auto;
		max-width: 34rem;
		font-size: 1rem;
	}

	.blocks {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}

	.block {
		background: var(--color-surface);
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		border-radius: 14px;
		padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
	}

	.block-title {
		margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		color: #ffae2e;
	}

	.block-text {
		margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
		font-size: 1rem;
	}

	.block-text:last-child {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	.block--example {
		text-align: center;
	}

	.compare-stack {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		margin: 0.9rem 0 0.5rem;
	}

	.compare-labeled-row {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.6rem;
	}

	.compare-row-label {
		min-width: 3.2rem;
		text-align: right;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.06em;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
	}

	.compare-row {
		display: flex;
		gap: 0.3rem;
	}

	.compare-tile {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		width: 2.2rem;
		height: 2.2rem;
		border-radius: 22%;
		border: 1px solid #4a3826;
		background: #1c140d;
		transition:
			border-color 0.15s ease,
			box-shadow 0.15s ease;
	}

	.compare-tile--on {
		border-color: #ffae2e;
		box-shadow: 0 0 10px color-mix(in srgb, #ffae2e 55%, transparent);
	}

	.compare-tile--diff {
		border-color: var(--color-danger);
		box-shadow: 0 0 10px color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-danger) 65%, transparent);
	}

	.compare-digit {
		width: 68%;
		height: 68%;
		overflow: visible;
	}

	.compare-segment {
		fill: #241a10;
	}

	.compare-tile:not(.compare-tile--on) .compare-segment.is-on {
		fill: #a8804f;
	}

	.compare-tile--on .compare-segment.is-on {
		fill: #fff3d6;
		filter:
			drop-shadow(0 0 3px #ffae2e)
			drop-shadow(0 0 8px #ffae2e);
	}

	.compare-caption {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		color: var(--color-danger);
	}

	.unit-list {
		display: inline-block;
		text-align: left;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0.8rem 1rem 0.8rem 1.6rem;
		border-radius: 12px;
		background: var(--color-bg);
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
	}

	.unit-list li {
		margin: 0.3rem 0;
	}

	.example-name {
		color: var(--color-text);
		font-weight: 700;
	}

	.learn-pagination {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
	}

	.learn-pagination-link {
		color: #ffae2e;
		font-weight: 600;
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	.learn-pagination-link:hover {
		text-decoration: underline;
	}

	.learn-pagination-next {
		margin-left: auto;
	}

	.learn-pagination-soon {
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
		font-weight: 600;
		font-style: italic;
	}
</style>
